            "  - A variable is a named memory location that stores a value.\n"
            "  - Python uses dynamic typing: variable types are inferred automatically at runtime.\n\n"
            "• Variable Naming Rules (PEP 8 Standards):\n"
            "  - Must begin with a letter (a-z, A-Z) or an underscore (_).\n"
            "  - Cannot begin with digits (e.g., 1st_user is INVALID; user_1 is VALID).\n"
            "  - May only contain alphanumeric characters and underscores.\n"
